    "answer": {
      "short": "$C(6,10),\\ D(6,4)$ or $C(-6,10),\\ D(-6,4)$.\n\nThe other side of the square lies 6 units to the right or left of $AB$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AB&=10-4\\\\AB&=6\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nA square has equal sides and right angles. Its area is $6\\times6=36\\text{ cm}^2$, so the horizontal sides extend 6 units either right or left of $AB$.\n\nTo the right: $C(6,10)$ and $D(6,4)$.\n\nTo the left: $C(-6,10)$ and $D(-6,4)$.",
